# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/502-route-sdlc-execute-against-the-fetched-remote-default-branch-instead-of-the-stale-local-ref/requirements.md
Feature: /sdlc-execute routes against the fetched remote default branch

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: An empty issue branch routes to implement despite a stale local default branch
    Given the local "main" is behind "origin/main"
    And the issue branch "42-example" was created from "origin/main" with no commits of its own
    When /sdlc-execute routes issue #42
    Then the implement worker is dispatched
    And prepare-version is not invoked before the implement worker starts

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A branch with real commits still routes to verify
    Given the local "main" is behind "origin/main"
    And the clean, published issue branch "42-example" has an implementation commit ahead of "origin/main"
    When /sdlc-execute routes issue #42
    Then prepare-version runs before the first worker
    And the verify worker is dispatched first

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: An unreadable remote default ref fails closed
    Given the fetch of "refs/heads/main" into "refs/remotes/origin/main" fails on issue branch "42-example"
    When /sdlc-execute routes issue #42
    Then the controller exits non-zero with "default_branch_unreadable" on stderr
    And no worker is started
    And prepare-version is not invoked

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Regression tests cover the stale local default branch
    Given scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs
    When "cd scripts && npm test" runs
    Then the stale-local-default empty-branch, real-commits and fetch-failure tests pass
